# F4 (2026-09-25): the blanket *.ttf rule above meant Inter-Medium.ttf -- a required build-time
# import in the T4 og-image generator (renderRoutePage's /og/* handler in src/index.js), embedded
# via wrangler.jsonc's "Data" rule for **/*.ttf, not fetched at runtime -- was never actually
# committed. A fresh clone of this repo could never build/deploy that handler at all (confirmed:
# `wrangler deploy --dry-run` failed with "Cannot find package './assets/Inter-Medium.ttf'").
# Whoever last deployed it successfully must have had this file locally, uncommitted. Real Inter
# Medium (SIL OFL, freely redistributable), sourced from Google's own google/fonts repository and
# instanced down to a genuinely static weight-500 TTF with fonttools (the variable font as
# published crashes this project's satori/opentype.js version on its fvar table -- confirmed by
# testing both before choosing the static instance). Same exception pattern as !.env.example above.
!src/assets/Inter-Medium.ttf
